    <string name="tutorial_step_count">Step %1$d of %2$d</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step1_title">Recognize the blocked setting</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step1_body">If Android shows “App was denied access” or “Controlled by restricted setting,” Black cannot turn Usage access on yet.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step2_title">Open Black app info</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step2_body">Return to Black’s App exceptions screen and tap “Open Black app info.”</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step3_title">Allow restricted settings</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step3_body">On Black’s App info page, open the three-dot menu and select “Allow restricted settings.” Confirm with your screen lock if asked. The menu appears only when Android has restricted this APK.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step4_title">Grant Usage access</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step4_body">Return to Black, tap “Grant usage access,” choose Black, and turn on “Permit access to app usage data.” The screenshot shows the switch before Android unlocks it.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step5_title">Check that exceptions are active</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step5_body">Return to App exceptions. The screen should say “Usage access granted. Automatic pausing is active.” You can now add apps to the exception list.</string>
